       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose. Going above the ceiling adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and it substantially raises the risk of GI hemorrhage, renal injury, and cardiovascular harm. I can't find a clinical scenario where that trade-off makes sense.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than that, you could add scheduled acetaminophen or another analgesic, or ask pharmacy to review. If you still want the 1600 mg dose, you'll need to enter it directly in the order system and go through pharmacy verification. I'd be glad to enter a lower dose now so the patient isn't left without an order."
